{"unit":3,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 3","tracks":{"a33":"Track_3.3.mp3","a35":"Track_3.5.mp3"},"SEGS":{"summary":["a33",4.08,null],"ed":["a35",3.75,null]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 3 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Rising to it</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 3, with four questions that come back from Units 1 and 2. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u3\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">The children who could not&hellip; the marshmallow covered their eyes.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">measure</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">resist</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">admire</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">He bought it without thinking about it at all &mdash; completely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">on schedule</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">full-time</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">on impulse</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">A chef has to plan several dishes at once, so the job is really about&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">multitasking</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">observing</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">rewarding</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">Nothing in the shop was worth the money. Everything was&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">computerized</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">overpriced</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">left-handed</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match each verb to the phrase it goes with. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"x1\">make</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"x2\">set</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"x3\">deal</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"x4\">give</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"x5\">take</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"x3\" data-short=\"with a problem\">with a problem</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"x5\" data-short=\"responsibility\">responsibility</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"x1\" data-short=\"an effort\">an effort</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"x4\" data-short=\"in\">in</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"x2\" data-short=\"goals\">goals</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each compound adjective with one word.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">She works nine to five, five days a week &mdash; it is a <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"full\" data-why=\"<b>Full-time</b> work.\"> -time job.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">I did not buy it new. It was <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"second\" data-why=\"<b>Second-hand</b> = not new.\"> -hand.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">The hotel is expensive because it is <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"five\" data-why=\"A <b>five-star</b> hotel.\"> -star.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">After four weeks he&hellip; convince the judges that he was a real chef.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">succeeded in</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">could to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">managed to</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">She&hellip; swimming before she was four years old.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">could swim</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">managed to swim</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">succeeded to swim</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">In a professional kitchen you&hellip; work to very precise times.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">don&rsquo;t have to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">have to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">are allowed to</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">A chauffeur&hellip; comment on anything the passenger says. It is completely forbidden.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">doesn&rsquo;t have to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">doesn&rsquo;t need to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">mustn&rsquo;t</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the words in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>succeed / turn</i>) The children who waited <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"succeeded in turning\" data-why=\"<b>Succeed in</b> + <i>-ing</i>.\"> their attention away from the plate.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>be able / finish</i>) I hope I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"will be able to finish|'ll be able to finish\" data-why=\"<i>Can</i> has no future form &rarr; <b>will be able to</b>.\"> it before Friday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>not have to</i>) In the burger van he <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"didn't have to|did not have to\" data-why=\"No obligation, in the past &rarr; <b>didn&rsquo;t have to</b>.\"> take much responsibility.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>allow</i>) Staff are not <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"allowed to use|allowed\" data-why=\"<b>Be allowed to</b> + base verb for permission.\"> their phones in the kitchen.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">In the end she <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"managed to finish\" data-why=\"<b>Manage</b> takes the infinitive: <i>managed to finish</i>.\"> the whole thing.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">After three attempts he <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"succeeded in passing\" data-why=\"<b>Succeed</b> takes <i>in</i> + <i>-ing</i>: <i>succeeded in passing</i>.\"> the test.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">You <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"don’t have to|do not have to\" data-why=\"No obligation is <b>don&rsquo;t have to</b>; <i>mustn&rsquo;t</i> means it is forbidden.\"> come in on Saturday if you don’t want to.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">It was difficult, but in the end I finished it.<br>In the end I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"managed to finish it\" data-why=\"<b>Manage to</b> = succeed after difficulty.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">It is not necessary for you to book a table.<br>You <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"don't have to book a table|do not have to book a table|don't need to book a table\" data-why=\"No obligation &rarr; <b>don&rsquo;t have to</b>.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">Photography is forbidden in this room. <i>(mustn&rsquo;t)</i><br>You <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"mustn't take photographs in this room|must not take photographs in this room|mustn't take photos in this room\" data-why=\"Forbidden &rarr; <b>mustn&rsquo;t</b>.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The four-minute barrier</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">For years, doctors said no human being could run a mile in under four minutes. Six weeks after somebody did, so did somebody else.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>By the early 1950s the four-minute mile had become the most famous unbroken record in sport. Runners had been getting closer for twenty-five years without managing to cross the line, and the failure had produced a comfortable explanation: the human body simply was not able to do it. Some newspapers reported, wrongly, that doctors believed the attempt would be dangerous.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>Roger Bannister was a medical student, which meant he could not train full-time. He ran in his lunch hour. What he had instead of hours was a method: he broke the distance into four separate races of one lap each and practised only the lap he was worst at. On 6 May 1954, in cold wind at Oxford, he succeeded in running the mile in three minutes and 59.4 seconds.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>The interesting part is what happened next. John Landy, an Australian who had been trying for years and never got below four minutes, managed it forty-six days later. Within three years, sixteen other runners had done the same. Nothing had changed about the human body in three years. What had changed was that everybody now knew it could be done.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>Sports psychologists still use the story, and they are careful about the lesson they take from it. It is not that belief alone makes people faster; Bannister trained, and trained cleverly. It is that a belief about what is impossible can quietly set the limit of what people are willing to attempt &mdash; and that limit is often the only thing holding the record in place.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">The main point of the text is that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">medical students make the best athletes</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">records are broken when equipment improves</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">what people believe is possible affects what they try</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">Why could Bannister not train full-time?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">he was not allowed to by his club</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">he was studying medicine</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">doctors had warned him it was dangerous</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">Bannister practised every lap equally. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: he practised <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">John Landy broke four minutes less than two months after Bannister. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph C: <b>True</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">Bannister and Landy became friends afterwards. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"The text says nothing about their relationship.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">The weather at Oxford that day was good. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: he ran <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph A, <i>a comfortable explanation</i> suggests that the idea was\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">easy to accept, and therefore not questioned</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">proved by careful research</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">invented by newspapers to sell copies</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">Why do psychologists say they are &ldquo;careful about the lesson&rdquo;?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">because the record was later found to be false</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">because belief without training does not make anybody faster</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">because only sixteen runners ever managed it</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play each recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('summary',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 1 &middot; the marshmallow study\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 3.3</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 1. True or false?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">A child who waited was given two marshmallows. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"The reward for waiting was <b>True</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">Most of the children found waiting easy. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Most of them gave in before the time was up.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">When the children were taught a technique, far more of them succeeded. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Nearly all of them managed to wait once they had been shown how.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('ed',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 2 &middot; Ed describes two jobs\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 3.5</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 2. Which job is each rule about?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">He does not have to work outside any more. <select data-answer=\"chef\" data-why=\"Working indoors belongs to the professional kitchen.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"van\">the burger van</option><option value=\"chef\">training as a chef</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">He did not have to take much responsibility. <select data-answer=\"van\" data-why=\"In the burger van his boss dealt with the money.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"van\">the burger van</option><option value=\"chef\">training as a chef</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">He has to manage a team. <select data-answer=\"chef\" data-why=\"Running a kitchen means managing people.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"van\">the burger van</option><option value=\"chef\">training as a chef</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">You are warning somebody about a step where people usually go wrong.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">And there you have it.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Be careful not to cut it too big.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Once you&rsquo;ve done that&hellip;</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You want to say that two things happen at the same time.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">After that, fill the bottle.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">The first thing you do is fill the bottle.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">While the glue is drying, fill the bottle.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You are the follower and you did not catch one step.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Can you say that part again?</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Finally, add more glue.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Make sure you don&rsquo;t overtighten it.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Where does each line belong &mdash; in spoken instructions, or in a written opinion paragraph?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Spoken\">Right, so the first thing you do is take the back off.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Written\">One reason is money; another is confidence.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Spoken\">Look, like this. See?</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Written\">To sum up, the benefit lasts far longer than the cost.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Spoken\"><h5>Spoken instructions</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Written\"><h5>Written opinion</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the five parts of the opinion paragraph in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"o4,o1,o3,o5,o2\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"o1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">One reason is money: a small repair often costs less than an hour of your time.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"o2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">To sum up, one afternoon of teaching saves money for forty years.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"o3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">For example, my neighbour nearly replaced a washing machine because of a blocked pipe.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"o4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I believe every school should teach at least one practical repair skill.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"o5\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Of course, not everybody will become an engineer.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Four of these gaps come back from Units 1 and 2. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Aigerim</b>How did the first week in the kitchen go?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Hard. On day one I <select data-answer=\"couldn&rsquo;t\" data-why=\"A general past inability &rarr; <b>couldn&rsquo;t</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>didn&rsquo;t manage</option><option>couldn&rsquo;t</option><option>wasn&rsquo;t allowed</option></select> even chop an onion at their speed.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Aigerim</b>And now?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>By Friday I <select data-answer=\"had managed to\" data-why=\"An achievement earlier than the moment we are describing &rarr; past perfect + <i>had managed to</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>had managed to</option><option>managed</option><option>have been managing</option></select> run a whole service on my own.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Aigerim</b>What is the hardest rule?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>You <select data-answer=\"mustn&rsquo;t\" data-why=\"Forbidden &rarr; <b>mustn&rsquo;t</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>don&rsquo;t have to</option><option>aren&rsquo;t able to</option><option>mustn&rsquo;t</option></select> explain yourself. A short instruction is not rudeness. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span> And I <select data-answer=\"have known\" data-why=\"A state from the past up to now &rarr; present perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>am knowing</option><option>have known</option><option>know since</option></select> the head chef since school, which makes it stranger.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Aigerim</b>Tell me one disaster.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"While I was carrying\" data-why=\"A long background action &rarr; past continuous. <b>While I was carrying</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>While I carried</option><option>While I had carried</option><option>While I was carrying</option></select> six plates, somebody opened the door into me. <select data-answer=\"Luckily,\" data-why=\"Good news that came by chance. <b>Luckily,</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Luckily,</option><option>Unfortunately,</option><option>Personally,</option></select> I only dropped one.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 100&ndash;120 words. Give yourself twenty minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Write one opinion paragraph on this statement: <i>&ldquo;Every school should teach at least one practical skill that is not tested on paper.&rdquo;</i> State your opinion in the first line, give two reasons, attach one real example to the first reason, admit the other side in half a sentence, and close by restating your opinion in different words.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"I believe that&hellip;   One reason is&hellip;   For example,&hellip;   Another reason is&hellip;   Of course,&hellip;   To sum up,&hellip;\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your paragraph must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>the opinion in the <b>first</b> line, not the last</li>\n        <li>two reasons, and one concrete example attached to one of them</li>\n        <li>one ability form: <b>can, could, be able to, manage to, succeed in</b></li>\n        <li>one obligation form: <b>have to, must, mustn&rsquo;t, be allowed to</b></li>\n        <li>a conclusion that restates the opinion without repeating the words</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; instruct, then argue</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Talk somebody through something you can do well &mdash; at least six steps, words only, no pictures. <b>Part B.</b> Then answer: <i>what is the hardest unwritten rule in a job or a class you know?</i> Say what you have to do, what you mustn&rsquo;t do, and what you don&rsquo;t have to do.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>a sequencer at the start, in the middle and at the end</li>\n        <li>one <i>While&hellip;</i> for two things happening at once</li>\n        <li>one warning with <i>Make sure you&hellip;</i> or <i>Be careful not to&hellip;</i></li>\n        <li>in Part B: <b>have to</b>, <b>mustn&rsquo;t</b> and <b>don&rsquo;t have to</b>, once each</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>The first thing you do is&hellip; &middot; Next,&hellip; &middot; Once you&rsquo;ve done that&hellip; &middot; While it&rsquo;s &hellip;ing&hellip; &middot; Make sure you&hellip; &middot; Finally,&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my opinion is in the first line, and nobody has to guess what I think</li>\n        <li>each reason has something behind it, not the same opinion said twice</li>\n        <li>my example is concrete &mdash; a real thing that really happened</li>\n        <li>my conclusion introduces no new argument</li>\n        <li>my instructions had at least six steps and three sequencers</li>\n        <li>I warned my listener about one step before they reached it</li>\n        <li>I used <i>have to</i>, <i>mustn&rsquo;t</i> and <i>don&rsquo;t have to</i> with three different meanings</li>\n        <li>I gave the instructions without showing anything</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}